    {
      "key": "e4cbacca-5b49-4141-b039-c19a5c12b1cc",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Which of the explorations and mini-lessons did you complete in the previous lesson?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Briefly recap the three explorations (AI as Campaign Manager; AI in Creative Writing ; and AI in Content Creation) and mini-lessons (Impact on Environment, Human Skills, and Artists) from the previous lesson.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e4cbacca-5b49-4141-b039-c19a5c12b1cc",
        "lesson_activity.key": "64a78e25-4540-4aa4-8827-ace37d484f66"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3274455f-ebe7-4c75-a740-10e5f3ae3630",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students will meet with both expert and jigsaw groups to share findings and begin synthesizing patterns that will become actionable guidance for co-creating with AI.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students take out their Milestone 2 Learning Log from the previous lesson and their KWL Chart from Lesson 1.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Organize students into their Expert Groups based on the specific exploration they completed in the previous lesson.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Jigsaw Synthesis"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3274455f-ebe7-4c75-a740-10e5f3ae3630",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ee33544a-a229-44a7-a77f-7cf22a653da5",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "First, meet with others who did the same exploration as you. You are the experts on that specific task.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ee33544a-a229-44a7-a77f-7cf22a653da5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e67f6c54-9a50-470e-8846-ab2a4125053f",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students reflect on their experiences with the previous exploration and consider one of the following questions:\n- At what point did the product become \"mostly AI\"?\n- When did it lose your personal \"voice\" or \"values\"?\n- What human input mattered most?\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Reform groups with members from different Explorations and Mini-Lessons. Explain expectations for sharing and note-taking using the Co-Pilot Debrief organizer."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e67f6c54-9a50-470e-8846-ab2a4125053f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3ca6182a-6930-40ed-83cd-53dffeea7340",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now we will transition into jigsaw group. Share one finding from your Expert Group. As a group, focus on patterns and rules you found rather than just retelling the steps that you went through.",
        "remarks": true,
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students to name specific evidence (an edit, a prompt change, or a missing emotional beat) that shows where human input mattered."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Listen for students articulating both a tipping point and a human necessity when sharing their examples."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3ca6182a-6930-40ed-83cd-53dffeea7340",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "77354415-4d18-4446-af48-3ad937fe95c8",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "77354415-4d18-4446-af48-3ad937fe95c8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ecae326a-24ef-4ad2-b51b-fb2774532bae",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students update their KWL Chart."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ecae326a-24ef-4ad2-b51b-fb2774532bae",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "53bcc78e-7955-47a6-ad85-c2e66a553258",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Choose one jigsaw learning from your Learning Log and write one or more responses in the KWL chart that reflects your new understanding or new questions.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "53bcc78e-7955-47a6-ad85-c2e66a553258",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "287ee813-ba0a-4faf-8835-375cfa3509cf",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who give very general answers and prompt them to add a specific example (for instance, a skill they'd keep vs. one they'd offload). For students who need support, offer a sentence stem from the organizer."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "287ee813-ba0a-4faf-8835-375cfa3509cf",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "655a7f94-0912-4ee9-bbeb-bf5103ede97e",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students apply their evidence to create clear, actionable guidelines for how they will use AI for the remainder of the course and in their final project.",
        "duration": "20",
        "name": "Project Work"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "655a7f94-0912-4ee9-bbeb-bf5103ede97e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a3ba5f55-6385-45f9-91fe-a2e556aaaaed",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Use your experience with your Explorations, Mini-Lessons, and your jigsaw conversations to draft a set of advice and guidelines that show how you will act as the Pilot and how you will use the AI as a Co-Pilot. Be specific: include a evidence from your testing.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a3ba5f55-6385-45f9-91fe-a2e556aaaaed",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8386eed8-4910-4abf-8997-39409166792d",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Students draft their Co-Creation with AI guidance, making choices about medium and selecting layouts from their Digital Gallery Walk (Lesson 2).",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Push for nuance – avoid \"never\" or \"always\" statements. Ask students to cite one example from their evidence to justify each guideline."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Check that each student's draft includes a Pilot Test and an AI Impact check and that at least one guideline ties to specific evidence from their exploration."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8386eed8-4910-4abf-8997-39409166792d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "957eed82-ed38-44e0-b029-bfaa2809d562",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "957eed82-ed38-44e0-b029-bfaa2809d562",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "10092d5c-738e-4388-bad7-ba019ffcc27f",
      "position": 13,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 4, Level 1. Students will begin drafting the Co-Creation with AI portion of their project.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for drafts that include (a) a clear evidence from explorations and mini-lessons, (b) rules, guidance, and advice that comes from those sources, and (c) a connections to specific conversations from the jigsaw. Prompt students who miss any of these to add one concrete example or check.",
        "progression_name": "Project Work - Milestone 2"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "10092d5c-738e-4388-bad7-ba019ffcc27f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4c2c6db6-3e27-4c75-8461-455840b2f240",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students add one new question that came up while working on the project to the Want to Know column of the KWL Chart.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who write superficial questions (for example, \"What is AI?\") and prompt them to make the question more specific (for example, \"How might AI change our community's creative work?\"). For students who are stuck, suggest they check their Co-Pilot Debrief notes for something that surprised them. For students who finish early, invite them to draft a brief action step they'd take to test their question.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Collect a quick sample of student KWL entries to check for depth—strong questions reference specific tensions (authorship, bias, skill development)."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4c2c6db6-3e27-4c75-8461-455840b2f240",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1d3d6b15-8679-4e84-b5aa-6d1168d4d904"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d405f955-5ed2-45f7-b9e2-22b219a5cab6",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d405f955-5ed2-45f7-b9e2-22b219a5cab6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1d3d6b15-8679-4e84-b5aa-6d1168d4d904"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5f9ab2b1-a1f3-4c55-9723-2ab88fa69868",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 4, Level 2 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5f9ab2b1-a1f3-4c55-9723-2ab88fa69868",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1d3d6b15-8679-4e84-b5aa-6d1168d4d904"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4242a5a8-82bc-478b-b84b-d558363d3e62",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Challenge students' confidence in spotting AI content and generate curiosity about how to verify digital information.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Which of these advertisement seems real? Why or why not?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** While both advertisements use realistic imagery and depictions of teens, neither is real. Ask students to point out details that seem out of place or slightly unnatural.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to move past examining the overall composition of an image and to zoom in on specific details to guide them in determining the images' credibility:\n- Image 1: Look at the fingers holding the candy and the text on the bag—it’s gibberish compared to the clean 'Fizzbites' logo. Also, notice the candy on her tongue looks like a blurry digital blob.\n- Image 2: Look at the crowd. The further back you go, the more the faces turn into melted features. Check the hands holding the bags; some have extra fingers or fingers that blend directly into the plastic."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4242a5a8-82bc-478b-b84b-d558363d3e62",
        "lesson_activity.key": "eb147d2a-5f52-4b0b-87e0-420243289f6e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f2aa8168-4928-40a9-bd8e-c77091a916cc",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f2aa8168-4928-40a9-bd8e-c77091a916cc",
        "lesson_activity.key": "eb147d2a-5f52-4b0b-87e0-420243289f6e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "aaee7f2b-1d8f-488d-909f-465145ba900c",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *credible*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *bias*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "aaee7f2b-1d8f-488d-909f-465145ba900c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "eb147d2a-5f52-4b0b-87e0-420243289f6e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3038387f-4206-4c06-aab0-ef42954f796c",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the Milestone 3 Learning Log.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the explorations by reading the inquiry question.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students choose a station and follow the instructions in Part 1 of the station Exploration Guide. They will record their ideas in the Collaborative Brainstorm section of the Milestone 3 Learning Log.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Consider timing this section so that the whole class can move into the follow-up synthesizing discussion as a group. Encourage students to be as specific as possible. The clearer their human vision, the easier it will be to spot when the AI deviates from it."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3038387f-4206-4c06-aab0-ef42954f796c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e300891d-78c7-4c6e-8684-251ddf4616b3",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e300891d-78c7-4c6e-8684-251ddf4616b3",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "22afa26c-8d8c-4680-a133-2b72cc91526e",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Is sounding confident the same as being correct?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students distinguish between confidence and accuracy, recognizing that the way information is presented — including by AI — can create a false sense of credibility even when the content is incomplete or wrong.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 5, Level 1 to choose a question they are interested in investigating.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Assist student in following the station Exploration Guide.",
        "progression_name": "Testing Truth and Credibility",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students should test in a rapid and iterative manner throughout this part of the exploration. The intent is for students to have multiple touches and to begin noticing patterns in the outputs"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "22afa26c-8d8c-4680-a133-2b72cc91526e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7cf93c0d-0f28-4964-b8a0-b39226efda77",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7cf93c0d-0f28-4964-b8a0-b39226efda77",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7dc99949-bf4b-4f40-b1fc-03fe7dd40aa5",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What do most of the responses AI gives you have in common?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students begin to recognize that AI consistently generates answers and images that sound confident and complete, even when information is missing or uncertain. They notice that confidence is part of the pattern AI produces — not proof of accuracy or understanding.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 5, Level 2 to complete Levels 2 and 3.\n- Level 2: Students use Sketch Lab to design their own 5-level Trust Meter that ranges from \"Highly Trustworthy\" to \"Falls Apart.\" Each level should include a short description explaining what makes an AI output land there (e.g., evidence included, missing details, assumptions, real-world accuracy).\n- Level 3: Students select between 'AI's Environmental Footprint,' 'Human Skill & AI Symbiosis,' or 'Training Data & Artist Rights.'\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Assist students with using Sketch Lab as needed. Push their thinking with questions such as:\n- What makes something move from Level 4 to Level 3?\n- How would you know if it’s missing important details?\n\nFor Level 3, ask students what surprised them. For the environment lesson, check if they understood the cooling requirements for server farms. For the skill lesson, ask them to define 'atrophy' in their own words. For artist rights, ask how they would feel if an AI learned from their work.",
        "progression_name": "Judge Truth and Credibility"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7dc99949-bf4b-4f40-b1fc-03fe7dd40aa5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "48b64f09-3172-4c5d-89a2-84d43aed0067",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Mini-Lessons: Testing Truth and Credibility",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Check whether students' scales reflect clear reasoning rather than gut reactions."
          },
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "After students apply their Trust Meters to an AI output, invite quick comparisons across groups. Differences in ratings create productive discussion and surface how trust is influenced by patterns, presentation style, and personal assumptions."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "48b64f09-3172-4c5d-89a2-84d43aed0067",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5e08302c-d742-4436-9f9d-789c25971901",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5e08302c-d742-4436-9f9d-789c25971901",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1f7056d9-c5b4-4272-8f75-4dd34bbecc4f",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now that you've seen the trade-offs, it's time to set your own rules. Every pilot needs a flight plan, and every creator needs ethical boundaries.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1f7056d9-c5b4-4272-8f75-4dd34bbecc4f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bea95f93-01f5-4a88-9e03-0dbafd9f39ce",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students document a learning, observation or question  from their mini-lesson in the class KWL Chart.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Check student responses for specific boundaries. A strong response identifies a specific task they will keep human-powered ('I will write the personal stories myself') rather than a vague statement."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bea95f93-01f5-4a88-9e03-0dbafd9f39ce",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d06a2320-dc91-4631-a094-d9b369248d87",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students reflect on how AI generates convincing responses and define personal strategies for evaluating credibility instead of relying on tone alone.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d06a2320-dc91-4631-a094-d9b369248d87",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1bbcac50-d51d-4c5a-8cae-98f445bb679d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "628475e5-6f0f-4252-b173-e4bba8355859",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Think back to today's explorations. When did AI sound most believable? When did that confidence break down? Where did you notice assumptions, missing context, or polished language without clear evidence? Decide what you will do in the future when something sounds convincing but may not be grounded.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "628475e5-6f0f-4252-b173-e4bba8355859",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1bbcac50-d51d-4c5a-8cae-98f445bb679d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a382631a-9fa1-44c3-9988-32157e48c611",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to draft their personal \"Truth and Credibility Guidelines\" in their Milestone 3 Learning Log using the provided sentence stem.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage specificity. Instead of writing \"I will check it,\" students might write:\n\n- \"I will look for named sources.\"\n- \"I will ask for risks or opposing views.\"\n- \"I will ask what information might be missing.\"\n- \"I will compare it with another source.\""
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a382631a-9fa1-44c3-9988-32157e48c611",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1bbcac50-d51d-4c5a-8cae-98f445bb679d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ecfd1b8b-3e02-4558-bb45-e0febfc9ea19",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ecfd1b8b-3e02-4558-bb45-e0febfc9ea19",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1bbcac50-d51d-4c5a-8cae-98f445bb679d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "56ef0a2f-1e3f-44ce-997d-cd2e1350ff5c",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the key vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "56ef0a2f-1e3f-44ce-997d-cd2e1350ff5c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1bbcac50-d51d-4c5a-8cae-98f445bb679d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5902b409-6ac3-41ad-a5c5-b39280018cf1",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 5, Level 4 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5902b409-6ac3-41ad-a5c5-b39280018cf1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1bbcac50-d51d-4c5a-8cae-98f445bb679d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "221d25a3-c899-4261-a1b8-39701fe6964c",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Help students reconnect with their previous explorations and mini-lessons to prepare for synthesizing their findings into project guidance.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What different explorations or mini-lessons did you complete in the last lesson?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Briefly recap the three explorations and mini-lessons from the previous lesson.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "221d25a3-c899-4261-a1b8-39701fe6964c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "82615cb9-1f7e-4642-8090-c67558c80c31"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b46bf3d6-ffc3-424d-bd92-dcc4251a08dc",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students will meet with both expert and jigsaw groups to share findings and begin synthesizing patterns that will become actionable guidance for trusting AI's credibility.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students take out their Milestone 3 Learning Log.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Organize students into their Expert Groups based on the specific exploration they completed in the previous lesson.",
        "name": "Jigsaw Synthesis"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b46bf3d6-ffc3-424d-bd92-dcc4251a08dc",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "00430970-abd8-4d5d-b9ff-834c1b1dc891",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "First, meet with others who did the same exploration as you. You are the experts on that specific task.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "00430970-abd8-4d5d-b9ff-834c1b1dc891",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e8e5e6cf-644a-4500-a8ad-94005aff64cc",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Reform groups with members from different Explorations and Mini-Lessons."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e8e5e6cf-644a-4500-a8ad-94005aff64cc",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b1595cf0-2153-47c8-b663-b7100e9bf135",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now we will transition into jigsaw group. Share one finding from your Expert Group. As a group, focus on patterns and rules you found rather than just retelling the steps that you went through.",
        "remarks": true,
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students to name specific evidence (an edit, a prompt change, or a missing emotional beat) that shows where human input mattered."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Listen for students articulating both a tipping point and a human necessity when sharing their examples."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b1595cf0-2153-47c8-b663-b7100e9bf135",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "73f7f6d2-99f4-4fb1-ab57-2f452da6ce4e",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "73f7f6d2-99f4-4fb1-ab57-2f452da6ce4e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c54b27fe-1075-462d-81b9-32a903e649d0",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students synthesize their exploration findings to design a clear, practical Trust Meter that helps others decide when to trust AI and when to slow down and verify.",
        "duration": "20",
        "name": "Project Work"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c54b27fe-1075-462d-81b9-32a903e649d0",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "199c7c27-2538-4811-b934-a178fe1bea50",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Use what you discovered in your Explorations, Mini-Lessons, and jigsaw conversations to design a Trust Meter for your AI Responsibility Guide. Your meter should show different levels of trust and clearly explain what moves an AI response up or down. Be specific — include evidence from your testing to justify why something belongs at each level.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "199c7c27-2538-4811-b934-a178fe1bea50",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "501e9184-89a5-424a-9c4a-80c56111c6f6",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Students create and add a Trust Meter visual to their project.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Push students beyond vague language like \"check it\" or \"don't trust everything.\" Ask:\n\n- What specifically should someone look for?\n- What detail made you lower your trust during testing?\n- What pattern kept showing up?\n- Encourage conditional thinking instead of absolute rules.\n"
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Look for a Trust Meter that clearly defines multiple levels of trust, includes at least two specific user actions, and references concrete evidence from the student’s exploration to justify their guidance."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "501e9184-89a5-424a-9c4a-80c56111c6f6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8d692aea-9a8f-47c3-a6a1-93756c10ddb1",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8d692aea-9a8f-47c3-a6a1-93756c10ddb1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1d1dbe4f-549d-45e7-b1b3-e3b07c27787f",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 6, Level 1. Students will add to the project they started in Lesson 3.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Push students past vague advice (\"just check it\") by asking what specifically someone should look for, what detail lowered their trust during testing, and what patterns kept showing up encourage conditional thinking instead of absolute rules.",
        "progression_name": "Project Work - Milestone 3 "
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1d1dbe4f-549d-45e7-b1b3-e3b07c27787f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "333f09c6-dc03-4728-b75f-1fe6e9a2a41e",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Project Work - Image Generation",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students will access to the same Sketch Lab level on which they have been working on throughout the unit. There is also an optional AI Chat level for students to use to generate images for use in their project as needed."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "333f09c6-dc03-4728-b75f-1fe6e9a2a41e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "56feea60-c504-47c0-a4db-09aa1c6cae7b",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *If AI is trained on lots of examples, what happens if most of those examples come from the same type of person?*\n- *What happens if certain groups, ideas, or experiences show up less in the data?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students recognize that AI outputs reflect the data they were trained on, and that when that data is unrepresentative, the result is a system with built-in bias that can misrepresent or exclude certain groups and perspectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "56feea60-c504-47c0-a4db-09aa1c6cae7b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "b935594c-6d1b-4b2e-a1b8-4629d26245bb"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "134910d0-6f5f-4b78-b2fd-356344c28e32",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 6, Level 3 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "134910d0-6f5f-4b78-b2fd-356344c28e32",
        "lesson_activity.key": "b935594c-6d1b-4b2e-a1b8-4629d26245bb"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "17a48065-19c4-4a46-80ac-67b51000c132",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students explore how small pieces of public data can be combined to reveal sensitive information through a high-stakes scenario."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "17a48065-19c4-4a46-80ac-67b51000c132",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b358988a-840a-4760-9ec0-2f257faacca7",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Imagine your favorite streamer suddenly stops broadcasting because someone showed up at their house. No one knew where they lived, but they posted one photo. How could that one photo lead someone straight to their door? Today we're starting with a mystery. A famous streamer named Z-Tech went dark because someone found their house using nothing but a selfie. We're going to see if we can figure out how that happened.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b358988a-840a-4760-9ec0-2f257faacca7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bf81aaad-d903-4712-b8c2-c75ad9a37c68",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** With a partner, students examine the selfie to find three specific details in the background that could be used to pinpoint Z-Tech's location.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who are looking past the person in the photo and at the background. Ask: \"What does that bus number tell you about the school district?\" or \"How many stores in this city carry that specific soda flavor?\"",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Consider zooming in on a few different areas of the sample selfie image so that students can see more detail."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bf81aaad-d903-4712-b8c2-c75ad9a37c68",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "cd8ee64d-a89c-4109-88eb-0fe1b75e5e68",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What could you determine from what you saw in the image?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should realize that small, seemingly \"public\" details (weather, a soda brand) can be combined by a motivated person—or an AI—to reveal \"private\" or \"sensitive\" information like a home address.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Listen for students using the word \"inference\" or describing how one piece of data connects to another."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "cd8ee64d-a89c-4109-88eb-0fe1b75e5e68",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5bc32a27-8afc-449c-98da-0f0515ee80d7",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5bc32a27-8afc-449c-98da-0f0515ee80d7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "905f684a-e552-4518-9685-0cf9fb1e3444",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "905f684a-e552-4518-9685-0cf9fb1e3444",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "aace2c2f-3e46-4f7f-a948-70dbc302eaea",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students select an exploration to uncover both the benefits of sharing data with AI and the hidden risks of data oversharing.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Explorations"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "aace2c2f-3e46-4f7f-a948-70dbc302eaea",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "53ea95bb-7983-4a24-af3e-4f04ef302e25",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now that we've seen how a single photo can reveal a location, let's look at the different types of data we generate every day.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "53ea95bb-7983-4a24-af3e-4f04ef302e25",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8e7439e1-e00b-4173-996c-c95087981687",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *public data*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *private data*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *sensitive data*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the explorations by reading the inquiry question.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Transition: Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 1. Students work with a partner at their station to complete a data classification activity in which they are asked to analyze different types of data, with differing contexts, and to sort it into public, private, and sensitive categories.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who are choosing different explorations. Ask: \"Why did you pick this specific topic?\" Have students justify their inclusion of certain pieces of data into the various categories."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8e7439e1-e00b-4173-996c-c95087981687",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7bc91ed3-beda-4902-aabd-9182c45b5775",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Safety and Privacy",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students should test in a rapid and iterative manner throughout this part of the exploration. The intent is for students to have multiple touches and to begin building evidence to support their assertions on how they might best co-create with AI."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7bc91ed3-beda-4902-aabd-9182c45b5775",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ae6548e8-7562-435d-b736-ab4ad9e3bf2d",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ae6548e8-7562-435d-b736-ab4ad9e3bf2d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ecf8bf9d-0cfe-40d0-a75c-d0b53993443b",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What patterns did you recognize that separate public, private, and sensitive data?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students can quickly share some ways that they classified data and how they chose to differentiate. Some sample patterns that they might identify include:\n- Public data: General preferences, fandoms, or regional pride that help you connect with others but don't put your safety at risk.  (gaming handle, social media likes, t-shirt style)\n- Private data: Information that is unique to you but doesn't necessarily reveal your location. It’s often used for security questions or official records (legal name, birth year, allergies)\n- Sensitive data: Data that reveals exactly where you are, where you live, or your daily routine (house number, wi-fi name)\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 2. Students test the AI Chat by providing the AI with different combinations of Public and Private Data and exploring the outputs in terms of privacy and safety.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask students what combinations of data that they are providing to the AI and to explain the different results that they have received.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *How much data did the AI need to feel \"personal\" and to provide good output?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Answers will vary; however, students should realize that while more data leads to better personalization, it also increases the risk of revealing sensitive patterns.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 3. Students will practice the strategy of anonymizing data and making judgments about the line between safety and security and good AI output.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Assist students with using Sketch Lab as needed. Ask questions about why they anonymized certain details, but did not change others.",
        "progression_name": "Safety and Privacy"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ecf8bf9d-0cfe-40d0-a75c-d0b53993443b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "db3f05f2-5e1d-4fd3-bf7a-d33842bc01c6",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 4. Students select between a mini-lesson to explore a topic of their choice.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask students what surprised them.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Mini-Lessons",
        "progression_name": "Mini-Lessons: Safety and Privacy",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If students finish early, encourage them to explore a second topic to add context and depth to their project."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "db3f05f2-5e1d-4fd3-bf7a-d33842bc01c6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
