        "lesson_activity.key": "be9a1cab-aad1-4c02-b1c6-61041caf8377"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "27387f39-94e4-4f46-80cd-98a57ead127d",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "As you finish, write one new question that came up while you worked today. This helps guide future learning.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "27387f39-94e4-4f46-80cd-98a57ead127d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "be9a1cab-aad1-4c02-b1c6-61041caf8377"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "db225bdf-5ca6-4dd3-9155-405511e9739b",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who write superficial questions (for example, \"What is AI?\") and prompt them to make the question more specific (for example, \"How might AI change our community's creative work?\"). For students who are stuck, suggest they check their Co-Pilot Debrief notes for something that surprised them. For students who finish early, invite them to draft a brief action step they'd take to test their question.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Collect a quick sample of student KWL entries to check for depth—strong questions reference specific tensions (authorship, bias, skill development)."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "db225bdf-5ca6-4dd3-9155-405511e9739b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "be9a1cab-aad1-4c02-b1c6-61041caf8377"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9145986b-9526-4120-a31b-65864f80fe6e",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 8, Level 3 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9145986b-9526-4120-a31b-65864f80fe6e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "be9a1cab-aad1-4c02-b1c6-61041caf8377"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d4a4b28f-a834-4226-82c8-16203d856616",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Students mark their current stance on a spectrum (1–5 scale of AI helpfulness/safety). This visually documents how their opinion has evolved through testing. Then, on their other hand, ask students to rate their stance when they started the unit."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d4a4b28f-a834-4226-82c8-16203d856616",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0cad6689-5fda-435a-bcbf-d24ab01ba6c0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "46dd42c6-558b-4ffa-a988-321f65bd8b3e",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "On a scale of 1 to 5, where 1 is 'AI is risky and unhelpful' and 5 is 'AI is safe and essential,' where do you land today? Hold up that amount of fingers on your left hand. Now, rate where you started when we began this unit by holding up that amount of fingers on the right hand.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "46dd42c6-558b-4ffa-a988-321f65bd8b3e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0cad6689-5fda-435a-bcbf-d24ab01ba6c0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "97cecc57-e2b6-434d-b3be-e60a4806721f",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *How has your perspective towards AI evolved throughout the unit?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should be able to articulate why their position shifted. A student moving from a 2 to a 4 because they learned about specific guardrails shows strong conceptual growth. Encourage students to pick a rule that came from a surprising result in their testing. These often make for the most defensible guidelines.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "97cecc57-e2b6-434d-b3be-e60a4806721f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0cad6689-5fda-435a-bcbf-d24ab01ba6c0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e8a2955b-af77-454c-8fdb-da0672e7bc9a",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Prompt students to take out their Learning Logs and to turn to Milestone 5."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e8a2955b-af77-454c-8fdb-da0672e7bc9a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "834835fe-b86f-4d0c-8c4f-d67696d80e4c",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "You'll choose one of three bots to review your guide. Each one has a specific personality designed to push back on your logic. Don't take it personally—their job is to help you find gaps in your evidence or rules.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "834835fe-b86f-4d0c-8c4f-d67696d80e4c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "abf3fed9-103b-4769-b226-90c18b3928e7",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain the three bot personas to the class.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to choose the persona they find most \"annoying\" or challenging, as that will likely provide the most useful feedback for strengthening their guide."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "abf3fed9-103b-4769-b226-90c18b3928e7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bd0b5848-765f-4850-b347-4618e0622e38",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bd0b5848-765f-4850-b347-4618e0622e38",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d7b7f0ef-9922-4286-88dc-acf777df3f91",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 9, Level 1 to complete Levels 1 and 2.\n- Level 1: The Sketch Lab level where students have been building their project\n- Level 2: A choice level where students will select one of the AI personas in order to get feedback on their guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who are getting frustrated by the bot's pushback. Remind them that the bot is supposed to be difficult. Ask: \"What specific rule is the bot questioning? How can you rephrase it or add evidence to make it harder to argue with?\" Watch for students who are just agreeing with the bot—challenge them to defend their original stance if they still believe in it.",
        "progression_name": "Project Work - Milestone 5"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d7b7f0ef-9922-4286-88dc-acf777df3f91",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f0796fb0-1c63-487b-8864-eaa6a8b7a3ef",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "AI Feedback Test",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Check that students are actually modifying their guides in response to the chat. A successful stress test results in clearer, more defensible rules."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f0796fb0-1c63-487b-8864-eaa6a8b7a3ef",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ffcadf0d-65fe-4c6a-93ef-2a18b87e7110",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ffcadf0d-65fe-4c6a-93ef-2a18b87e7110",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "960c4ed9-08bc-4e00-900c-907e6f4812c6",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What was one suggestion from the AI bot that was logically correct but felt \"fake\" or wrong for a middle school audience?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students recognize that while AI is good at logic, it often lacks \"human nuance\"—the ability to understand tone, social context, or what actually resonates with people their age. This sets the stage for the peer review activity."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "960c4ed9-08bc-4e00-900c-907e6f4812c6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a9281568-10fd-4a8b-8d8d-e0fbe2ee2771",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students practice providing and receiving peer feedback in order to contrast the usefulness and effectiveness as compared to AI.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Peer Review Triangles"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a9281568-10fd-4a8b-8d8d-e0fbe2ee2771",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f4d87c8e-5789-4505-bf36-3770a706312d",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now that the AI has provided feedback, it's time for peers to provide their thoughts as well. AI is great at spotting logical gaps, but it can't tell you if your writing sounds like a robot wrote it or if a visual is confusing. We'll work in groups of three, with each person taking a specific role.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f4d87c8e-5789-4505-bf36-3770a706312d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6f730092-605c-453c-b03e-8f45048dc73b",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Assign students into groups of three and explain the roles.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students rotate between guides that are displayed on student computers so everyone gets feedback from a Reader, a Skeptic, and a Designer.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Listen for specific feedback. Are the \"Skeptics\" actually looking at the evidence from previous lessons? Are \"Readers\" identifying jargon that needs to be simplified? Probing question: \"How does this peer feedback differ from what the chatbot told you?\"",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If groups are uneven, a group of four can have two \"Readers\" focusing on different sections of the guide."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6f730092-605c-453c-b03e-8f45048dc73b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9b8acfdf-f5af-4a81-a0a5-0825ea1c45d1",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9b8acfdf-f5af-4a81-a0a5-0825ea1c45d1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9abff7a7-c99e-4365-9559-56efcad0b48a",
      "position": 13,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *In what ways can a human peer understand your reasoning differently than AI can?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students identify that humans understand intent, shared experiences, and emotional resonance. A peer knows what a middle schooler finds funny or confusing in a way a LLM cannot truly replicate."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9abff7a7-c99e-4365-9559-56efcad0b48a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "06a1c8fb-391a-4bec-be83-e8bde6693ed3",
      "position": 14,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students finalize their their guide's visuals in preparation for the final presentation.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Finalizing the Product"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "06a1c8fb-391a-4bec-be83-e8bde6693ed3",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "92a59de6-e10c-4fa7-a054-708c54ff058a",
      "position": 15,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Most people don't want to read a wall of text. They want to see at a glance if a tool is safe or helpful. See if you can add visuals to your guide that makes your conclusions and advice clear instantly. For instance, you might use a traffic light system or even a scale showing how much of the work was human vs. AI.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "92a59de6-e10c-4fa7-a054-708c54ff058a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bf7f29ce-a07d-4c5a-86cc-30157b0f5458",
      "position": 16,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 9, Level 3. Students work independently to finish their guides. Using AI Chat, they can create icons to support visually communicating their guidance and advice.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Assist students with composing prompts in order to get better image outputs.",
        "progression_name": "Project Work - Image Generation",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "The final product should demonstrate a clear visual rating system and incorporate feedback from both the AI stress test and peer review."
          },
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "For students struggling with the visual system, suggest they return to the Digital Gallery Walk that they conducted to explore different types of guides in Lesson 2."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bf7f29ce-a07d-4c5a-86cc-30157b0f5458",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bfe01452-c737-44ed-b366-0923dc3a76a5",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bfe01452-c737-44ed-b366-0923dc3a76a5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6b29878b-22d7-4932-80f3-f3f33fcf2710"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "caa7af8b-2479-4e14-9938-02c63dcc120a",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "To wrap up today, I want you to think about the two types of feedback you received. One came from a machine programmed to find logical gaps, and the other came from a human who understands your audience and context. Sometimes, hearing the truth from a bot feels different than hearing it from a friend.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "caa7af8b-2479-4e14-9938-02c63dcc120a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6b29878b-22d7-4932-80f3-f3f33fcf2710"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6b312089-f19e-45c7-8dae-eac3ee86fe71",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students respond to the prompt in their learning logs: AI vs. Human: Which feedback was harder to hear: the AI's logical pushback or your peer's skepticism? Why?\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who are reflecting on the 'nuance' of human feedback vs. the 'logic' of AI. Some may find the AI easier to handle because it lacks emotion, while others may find peer skepticism more helpful because it feels more authentic.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Review student entries to see if they can articulate the specific strengths of both feedback sources. Correct understanding identifies that AI is excellent for identifying missing data or logical errors, while humans are better at evaluating tone, relatability, and social impact."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6b312089-f19e-45c7-8dae-eac3ee86fe71",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6b29878b-22d7-4932-80f3-f3f33fcf2710"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9af60cf1-fc7c-4efe-93d2-22d92367a6e4",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9af60cf1-fc7c-4efe-93d2-22d92367a6e4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6b29878b-22d7-4932-80f3-f3f33fcf2710"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "410b0da5-0b6b-43e4-869f-1495b386c2b7",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 9, Level 4 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "410b0da5-0b6b-43e4-869f-1495b386c2b7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6b29878b-22d7-4932-80f3-f3f33fcf2710"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7a654d75-390a-4b19-a6f7-0c16d74d9a51",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students put finishing touches on their AI guidance project using the project checklist and rubric."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7a654d75-390a-4b19-a6f7-0c16d74d9a51",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ee699646-156e-4a25-85be-1869aea0720f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "77e14c9d-060f-405f-9846-aa00977c6b28",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Use the project checklist and rubric to make targeted final edits now. Focus on clear evidence, accurate descriptions of AI limitations, and concrete guidance for users. You have about ten minutes—make changes that strengthen your claim and examples.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "77e14c9d-060f-405f-9846-aa00977c6b28",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ee699646-156e-4a25-85be-1869aea0720f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c4aa7c0e-afd3-46dd-b5c3-915668598d52",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Ask students to complete these three steps:\n1. Open their AI guidance project in Lesson 10 Level 1.\n1. Review the project checklist and apply any missing elements.\n1. Use the rubric to make final edits, then save for final submission\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who (a) clearly cite evidence from prior investigations, (b) explain AI limitations (bias, hallucinations, missing context), and (c) provide concrete, actionable guidance for users. Common misconception: students may claim AI understands content—prompt them to reword this as pattern-based predictions. Ask probing questions: \"Which investigation supports this claim?\" \"How would a user apply this guidance in a real situation?\" Support strategies: suggest one high-impact edit (clarify a claim, add a citation, or add a limitation-and-mitigation note). For fast finishers: ask them to add a counterargument and brief rebuttal or to run a quick peer review with a partner.",
        "progression_name": "Final Project",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Listen for students naming specific investigations as evidence (e.g., bias exploration, hallucination example). Correct understanding includes: linking a claim to an investigation and describing a limitation plus a mitigation. If a student only states opinions without evidence, prompt: \"What data or example from our unit supports that?\""
          },
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that concise, evidence-based recommendations are stronger than broad statements. If time is tight, have students prioritize adding one clear example and one explicit mitigation strategy. Encourage peer checking: quick pair reviews catch unclear language and missing citations."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c4aa7c0e-afd3-46dd-b5c3-915668598d52",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ee699646-156e-4a25-85be-1869aea0720f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0cffabd7-d08b-4fdb-a580-0161349d21e9",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0cffabd7-d08b-4fdb-a580-0161349d21e9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ee699646-156e-4a25-85be-1869aea0720f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3be5c5e3-9641-4ea2-aef6-191f7d525b17",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3be5c5e3-9641-4ea2-aef6-191f7d525b17",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ee699646-156e-4a25-85be-1869aea0720f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "61f55db7-3960-475d-8d41-afef933ec04e",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today, you are defending a position about how humans should interact with AI.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "61f55db7-3960-475d-8d41-afef933ec04e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ee699646-156e-4a25-85be-1869aea0720f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0dd19256-6314-42db-87f5-ba362aee272a",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain each position and give a short classroom example (e.g., using AI to draft a quick email vs. editing AI-drafted email for accuracy and tone).",
        "progression_name": "Final Project",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Assign roles so each student practices both proposing and critiquing evidence across rounds."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0dd19256-6314-42db-87f5-ba362aee272a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6f68648d-7fdb-4f71-bfad-c02128f175d8",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6f68648d-7fdb-4f71-bfad-c02128f175d8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c1cc8da9-c1ff-4a1e-bb74-051dfe336dc9",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define human oversight.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of The Final Verdict activity guide."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c1cc8da9-c1ff-4a1e-bb74-051dfe336dc9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c22579c9-8707-46d6-b771-3dc9a5d7e5b7",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today you'll take part in a mini mock trial where you defend a position about how humans should interact with AI. Focus on clear claims and specific evidence from our unit.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c22579c9-8707-46d6-b771-3dc9a5d7e5b7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e77c6368-4f66-42bf-b94f-2b85877e04a7",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Read the slide aloud and confirm students understand the trial flow and time constraints.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Keep the trial tightly scoped and time-box each phase (opening, evidence, cross-exam, deliberation) so the activity stays quick and focused."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Listen for students describing the trial stages in correct order and naming at least one type of evidence they might use (credibility breakdown, bias example, privacy test)."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e77c6368-4f66-42bf-b94f-2b85877e04a7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e7377f36-2bee-44ba-b4a1-e474347a0e8b",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e7377f36-2bee-44ba-b4a1-e474347a0e8b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "95b80c55-db3a-449e-81c1-01ecc8877449",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today you'll take part in a mini mock trial where you defend a position about how humans should interact with AI. Focus on clear claims and specific evidence from our unit. The trial follows a short script: each side gives an opening statement, presents evidence with a short cross-exam, and then the jury deliberates and decides.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "95b80c55-db3a-449e-81c1-01ecc8877449",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0645ba30-4d29-4830-934f-2ab73e5d3c41",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Walk students through each stage and show timing expectations (for example: 1 minute opening, 1 minute per evidence, 1 minute cross-exam, 5 minute jury).",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Model strict timing and signal time warnings. If class size is large, run paired mini-trials or have the teacher act as one side so everyone practices roles."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0645ba30-4d29-4830-934f-2ab73e5d3c41",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "76eb6462-87c0-49fd-9f1b-055c30a6a8f1",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "76eb6462-87c0-49fd-9f1b-055c30a6a8f1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ecf67c77-4ded-496f-ba4c-9b7a7fb499f4",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Summarize the class verdict and highlight examples that show why human judgment matters (bias, hallucination, data inference, credibility checks).",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Reinforce nuance: acknowledge benefits of AI for speed and scale while stressing when oversight is needed. Invite students to suggest one classroom guideline for using AI responsibly going forward."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Ask students to briefly reflect: can AI ever be fully trusted without human checks? Look for answers that cite specific risks or evidence from the unit (e.g., hallucinations, biased data)."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ecf67c77-4ded-496f-ba4c-9b7a7fb499f4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d1820aaa-72eb-4bc6-b248-334beb1e3716",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *How did your thinking about AI's capabilities, limitations, or risks change during this unit?*\n- *What uncertainties or questions do you still have about when humans should rely on AI?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Surface how students' views shifted from simple judgments (AI is good/bad) to more nuanced positions that weigh benefits and risks. Listen for responses that reference specific investigations (bias, hallucinations, data privacy, co-creation). If discussion stalls, prompt: \"Which investigation surprised you most, and why?\" or \"What would make you trust an AI recommendation more?\"",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to respond to each other briefly (one follow-up question or connection). If time is tight, limit to two students per prompt and collect quick takeaways on the board."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d1820aaa-72eb-4bc6-b248-334beb1e3716",
        "lesson_activity.key": "549fdff2-91bf-441f-a5f0-204f08749bad"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3896cafb-1e39-40ff-809a-1c44b85c4da3",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3896cafb-1e39-40ff-809a-1c44b85c4da3",
        "lesson_activity.key": "549fdff2-91bf-441f-a5f0-204f08749bad"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a20104c7-f92c-43a8-a39d-33799a6588d4",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students write a short exit ticket (two to three sentences): first state their claim about how humans should interact with AI, then cite one piece of evidence from the unit that supports that claim."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a20104c7-f92c-43a8-a39d-33799a6588d4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "549fdff2-91bf-441f-a5f0-204f08749bad"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4f34c726-1742-4272-960b-946593dccd0a",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "For your exit ticket, briefly state your claim about how people should use AI and include one specific piece of evidence from our unit that supports that claim. Keep it short—two to three sentences.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4f34c726-1742-4272-960b-946593dccd0a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "549fdff2-91bf-441f-a5f0-204f08749bad"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "51f54daf-0e17-499b-aca8-f81bce70a032",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for clear claims and a connected piece of evidence. Common issues: students may restate an opinion without evidence, or they may cite vague evidence (e.g., \"we did experiments\"). Ask probing questions: \"Which investigation are you referencing? What did it show?\" Support strategies: for students who struggle, prompt them with examples (bias exploration, hallucination examples, privacy test, co-creation demo). For advanced students, ask them to add a brief qualifier (e.g., \"usually\" or \"in cases where...\").",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for clear claims and a connected piece of evidence. Common issues: students may restate an opinion without evidence, or they may cite vague evidence (e.g., \"we did experiments\"). Ask probing questions: \"Which investigation are you referencing? What did it show?\" Support strategies: for students who struggle, prompt them with examples (bias exploration, hallucination examples, privacy test, co-creation demo). For advanced students, ask them to add a brief qualifier (e.g., \"usually\" or \"in cases where...\")."
          },
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If time is limited, collect responses digitally (Google Form) or have students drop their paper exit ticket in a tray as they leave. Use a few exemplar responses to start tomorrow's discussion."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "51f54daf-0e17-499b-aca8-f81bce70a032",
        "lesson_activity.key": "549fdff2-91bf-441f-a5f0-204f08749bad"
      }
    },
